===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₁rewdʰ-}}
From {{bor|en|la|rubellus|t=reddish}}, diminutive of {{m|la|ruber|t=red}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₁rewdʰ-}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹuːˈbɛlə/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛlə|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|pathology}} A mild disease caused by the {{taxlink|Rubella virus|species|ver=160928}} infecting the [[respiratory tract]], and characterised by a rash of pink dots, fever and swollen [[lymph node]]s.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|mild disease}} {{l|en|epidemic roseola}}, {{l|en|French measles}}, {{l|en|German measles}}, {{l|en|Liberty measles}}, {{l|en|three-day measles}}, {{l|en|3-day measles}}, {{l|en|false measles}}

